# Phase 4 Walkthrough: Node.js Express ⟷ Python FastAPI AI Bridge

## Summary of Changes
In **Phase 4**, the Node.js Express API Gateway was connected to the Python FastAPI AI microservice over HTTP REST, exposing `POST /api/predict` to receive base64 camera frames from frontend clients, forward them to the Python inference pipeline, and return real-time ISL alphabet predictions (`A`–`Z`) with confidence scores.

---

## 1. Key Components Created / Modified

- **[aiService.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/server/src/services/aiService.js)**:
  - Dynamically reads `process.env.AI_SERVICE_URL` (defaulting to `http://127.0.0.1:8000`).
  - Dispatches `POST /predict` requests with 10-second timeout handling.
- **[predictController.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/server/src/controllers/predictController.js)**:
  - Validates `req.body.image` (rejects missing/empty frames with HTTP 400).
  - Forwards frame to Python and returns prediction payload.
  - Implements defensive error boundaries:
    - `ECONNREFUSED` $\to$ HTTP 503 Service Unavailable (clear notification when Python is offline).
    - `ECONNABORTED` / timeout $\to$ HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout.
    - Upstream errors $\to$ forwards status code and message.
- **[predictRoutes.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/server/src/routes/predictRoutes.js)**:
  - Express router mounting `POST /api/predict`.
- **[server.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/server/src/server.js)**:
  - Mounted `/api/predict` and `/api/translate/predict` routes.
  - Increased JSON payload body limit to `15mb` to comfortably support high-resolution base64 video frames.
- **[client/src/services/api.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/client/src/services/api.js)**:
  - Added `sendPredictionFrame(base64Image)` for frontend consumption.
- **[test_bridge.js](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/server/tests/test_bridge.js)**:
  - Verification script testing both the health bridge (`GET /api/health/ai`) and live prediction bridge (`POST /api/predict`).

